A deliberate exception to the repository default of AGPL-3.0-only. These are the normative
integration contracts under `contracts/v1/` — JSON schemas, capability and compatibility
declarations, invariants, and fixtures. An integration author writes against them, so they
must be implementable by anyone in any software, including closed-source.

The directory contains data, not code: there is nothing here that can import anything, so
the dependency-direction rule is satisfied structurally. The traffic runs the other way —
`scripts/integration-contracts*.mjs` on the AGPL side READS these contracts, which is the
permitted direction (AGPL may absorb Apache-2.0; the reverse is the violation). See
../../LICENSING.md.

No third-party components.
